Template: orbiq-system-monitor/mqtt_broker
Type: string
Default:
Description: MQTT broker host name or IP address:
 OrbIQ publishes its sensors to this MQTT broker, for example the one Home
 Assistant uses. Enter a host name or an IP address, without "mqtt://" or a
 port.
 .
 Leave it empty to configure /etc/orbiq_system_monitor/config.toml by hand
 later. The service is not started without a broker.

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/mqtt_tls
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Connect to the broker with TLS?
 Choose yes if the broker has a TLS listener (usually port 8883). The broker
 certificate is checked against the system CA certificates, or against a CA
 file you name in the next question.

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/mqtt_port
Type: string
Default: 1883
Description: MQTT broker port:
 The default MQTT port is 1883, or 8883 with TLS.

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/mqtt_ca_file
Type: string
Default:
Description: CA certificate file for the broker (optional):
 Path to a PEM file with the CA that signed the broker certificate, for
 example a self-signed homelab CA. Leave it empty to use the system CA
 certificates.
 .
 For client certificates (mutual TLS), set client_cert_file and
 client_key_file in /etc/orbiq_system_monitor/config.toml.

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/mqtt_port_invalid
Type: error
Description: Invalid port
 The port must be a number from 1 to 65535.

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/mqtt_username
Type: string
Default:
Description: MQTT user name:
 Leave it empty if the broker allows anonymous connections.

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/mqtt_password
Type: password
Description: MQTT password:
 The password is written to /etc/orbiq_system_monitor/config.toml (readable
 by root only) and is not kept in the debconf database.

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/device_name
Type: string
Default:
Description: Device name:
 The name of this machine in Home Assistant. It is part of every MQTT topic
 and entity ID, so use only letters, digits, "-" and "_".

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/device_name_invalid
Type: error
Description: Invalid device name
 Use only letters, digits, "-" and "_".

Template: orbiq-system-monitor/enable_service
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Start OrbIQ now and on every boot?
 If you choose no, start it later with:
 systemctl enable --now orbiq_system_monitor
